    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1065">

                <pb facs="1095" n="809" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg809"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the German Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bernstorff</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-04-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I beg to acknowledge
                    the receipt of your two notes of April 18 informing me that certain official
                    papers belonging to the German Embassy were seized at the time of the arrest of
                    Mr. von Igel, and asking that the papers be returned to you immediately and not
                    examined or copied by any American official.</p>
                <p>In reply I beg to refer to our conversation of yesterday and to inform you again
                    that instructions were given immediately in regard to the return of the papers
                    to you.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
